  "sources": [
    {
      "url": "https://sfplanninggis.org/docs/landmarks_and_districts/LM100.pdf",
      "inspection": "Primary2023fact sheet pp29–31/exterior features read; PDFp49visuals actually inspected. About100ft front, unfinished concrete shell/ornamented3partstucco west face, giant arched mullioned light blind above mezzanine/2smallerlights, raised peak/sidepanels. Buff/pale pink palette. Deep arcade/island booth/5glazed oak doorpairs/blue tilebases/orange quarrypaving.1937blade nearly40ft tall/two identical red-white-blue-gold sides; marquee about12ft abovegrade/12ftprojection/30ftfront with45degree angled ends/bulbs.2019wide photo confirms flat skyline/caps and curb slope;2022foyer photos show3poster recesses on northwall, dark wood entryframes and freestanding faceted glazed booth with tiled base/overhanging dark top. Nominal measures/proportions, not threshold survey."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://www.google.com/maps/@37.76202,-122.43472,20z/data=!3m1!1e3",
      "inspection": "Current aerial actually inspected: historic theater has broad CastroStreetfront bar and narrower rear rectangular auditorium roof. Westblade/canopy project separately; neighboring lower shops/residences/USBank/parking are separate. Roof almostflat/crowned with sparse service equipment; local2016elevated image gives original mass/side pier rhythm. Current aerial does not supply surveyed heights or finished restoration color."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://thecastro.com/",
      "inspection": "Current owner-operated official calendar read and linked from AnotherPlanet venue page; active2026programming. Model is explicitly dated2008–2016local-corpus exterior, not a claim that all finishes/roof equipment/entry details match post-renovation2026."
    }
